# Python Code Style

## Runtime
- Use Python `3.10+` compatible syntax and stdlib usage.

## Style
- Follow PEP8 strictly.
- Keep max line length at `88` (Black-compatible).

## Typing
- Every function must include parameter and return type hints.
- Avoid untyped public APIs.

## Docstrings
- Use Google-style docstrings.
- Require docstrings for all public methods/functions/classes.
